# Obsidian Brain MCP Configuration
# Export these values before starting the server or add them to your MCP
# client's `env` configuration. The server does not load .env files itself.
#
# The server runs JavaScript inside the running Obsidian app through the
# registered CLI's `eval` command. Prerequisites:
#   - Obsidian 1.12.4+ is open with the target vault loaded.
#   - Settings > General > Advanced > "Command line interface" is on, and you
#     accepted the prompt to register it in PATH. Linux copies the bundled
#     `obsidian-cli` to ~/.local/bin/obsidian (mode 755; keep that on PATH),
#     Windows appends the install directory to the user PATH, macOS links it
#     into /usr/local/bin. Verify with `obsidian version`, which prints e.g.
#     `1.15.1 (installer 1.15.0)`.
#   - For get_daily_note / append_to_daily: the "Daily notes" core plugin is
#     enabled (Settings > Core plugins); its folder, format and template are used.

# Vault resolution order:
# 1) vault= argument sent when OBSIDIAN_VAULT is set
# 2) calling process CWD when it is inside a registered vault
# 3) most recently focused open vault window
# 4) otherwise: Vault not found.
# Set OBSIDIAN_VAULT to the vault folder name for reliability; Obsidian opens
# that vault's window on demand. A vault id from Obsidian's registry also works
# (see the README for the per-platform registry location).

# Optional: vault folder name or id, not a filesystem path.
# OBSIDIAN_VAULT=My Vault

# Optional: executable path when the CLI is not on PATH.
# OBSIDIAN_CLI_PATH=/full/path/to/obsidian

# Tests only: disposable vault for `pytest -m obsidian`. The name must contain
# "testvault"; the live tests refuse any other vault.
# OBSIDIAN_TEST_VAULT=my-testvault
